course: dictionary
lesson: 5028
title: Who lives there? Meet inhabit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To inhabit a place means to live in it. «Polar bears inhabit the Arctic» tells you that polar bears live there. The sentence is about where they live, so the word fits with homes and animals.
explain: Try the swap check. Put «live in» in place of «inhabit» and read it again: «Polar bears live in the Arctic» still makes sense. In a science lesson, «Which animals inhabit the rainforest?» asks which animals live in the rainforest.
explain: Inhabit can also be formal and mean to be present in something. «Strange creatures inhabit her stories» does not mean the creatures live in a house. It means they appear in her stories, so the word is about being there.
explain: Look at the word family. An inhabitant is a person or animal that lives somewhere. A habitat is the natural home of a living thing. Uninhabited means with nobody living there, as in «an uninhabited island».
fact: Inhabit means to live in a place.
fact: Inhabit is a verb, so it changes: inhabits, inhabited, inhabiting.
fact: An inhabitant is a person or animal that lives somewhere.
fact: A habitat is the natural home of a living thing.
fact: Uninhabited means with nobody living there, as in «an uninhabited island».
exercise: «Polar bears inhabit the Arctic.» What does inhabit mean here? | To dig up | To swim across | *To live in | To visit for one day
exercise: Find the word that means a person or animal that lives somewhere. | habitat | uninhabited | inhabiting | *inhabitant
exercise: «An uninhabited island» is an island where... | it has a big city | *nobody lives | it is in the Arctic | lots of people live
test: «Strange creatures inhabit her stories.» What does inhabit mean here? | *To be present in something | To run away from something | To buy something
test: Which word means the natural home of a living thing? | habit | uninhabited | inhabitant | *habitat
exam: «The town has ten thousand inhabitants.» What does inhabitants mean here? | The shops in the town | The roads that lead out of town | *The people who live there | The buildings in the town
